The assertion in this test is too weak. It only checks that an element has focus, but doesn't verify that the focus has correctly wrapped from the last to the *first* focusable element in the dialog. To make this test more robust, you should assert that `document.activeElement` is the specific first element.

```suggestion
    fireEvent.keyDown(document, { key: "Tab", shiftKey: false });
    // Focus should wrap to the first focusable element
    expect(document.activeElement).toBe(buttons[0]);
```

